//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Package
// $Module name: FTThemeColors
// $Author     : Nils Svedmyr, RDC Tools International, <mailto:support@rdctools.com>
// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
// Created     : 2026-08-13
//
// Description : Runtime colours for the NATIVE side of the FlexTron surface.
//
//               The web surface follows the theme through palette.css (--dfr-* under body.df-Light), but the
//               panels, hosts and margins around it are painted by DataFlex with clDarkWebBg / clDarkViewBg /
//               clDarkThemeText - compile-time Defines, which cannot vary at runtime. So in light mode the web
//               content went light and the native chrome stayed dark, which shows wherever a host does not fully
//               cover its panel: the gaps around a control, and any strip below the last web control (Nils
//               2026-08-13, the Add-a-package dialog: "the part with the Search for control and buttons, and
//               under them - the background is dark").
//
//               Every colour VALUE is a Define in FTConstants.h.pkg - the clDark* and clLight* pairs. These
//               functions only choose between them by the theme the program runs in, which a Define cannot do.
//               The CSS and WebView2 spellings of a colour come from its Define too (FTColorHex).
//
//               These read giFTThemeMode ONLY - deliberately no ghoApplication. A Global function must be
//               DEFINED above every caller, and ghoApplication is not declared until cRefactorApplication.pkg is
//               Used, far below the point where this has to be available. giFTThemeMode and the cl* constants
//               both come from FTConstants.h.pkg, which this package Uses itself (until 2026-09-23 they were in
//               RefactorConstants.h.pkg), so it can sit near the top of a program and be visible to everything.
//
//               Unseeded (CI_FTThemeUnset, the value before any FlexTron host has constructed) falls back to the
//               dark constants - the look the app has always had. The panels that call these do so in
//               End_Construct_Object, which runs after their hosts, so by then the global is seeded.
//
//               CI_FTThemeSystem returns the DARK values: "follow Windows" is resolved client-side by the
//               framework from prefers-color-scheme, and nothing native has read the OS preference. A user on
//               Follow-Windows-with-a-light-desktop therefore gets light web content in dark native chrome; if
//               that matters, the fix is to read AppsUseLightTheme from the registry here, not to guess.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use FTConstants.h.pkg           // giFTThemeMode, CI_FTTheme* and the clDark* colours
Use cCJCommandBarSystem.pkg     // xtpThemeVisualStudio2022Light / 2017Dark - FTCJTheme
Use cCJGridControl.pkg          // xtpGridThemeVisualStudio2012Light / Dark - FTCJGridTheme

// Two hex digits of a byte (0-255).
Function FTHexByte Global Integer iByte Returns String
    String sDigits
    Move "0123456789ABCDEF" to sDigits
    Function_Return (Mid(sDigits, 1, ((iByte iand 240) / 16) + 1) + Mid(sDigits, 1, (iByte iand 15) + 1))
End_Function

// "RRGGBB" of a DataFlex colour. RGB() keeps red in the LOW byte (the value is 00BBGGRR); CSS and WebView2
// want red first. The CSS and WebView2 spellings of a colour come from here, never from a second literal.
Function FTColorHex Global Integer iColor Returns String
    Function_Return (FTHexByte(iColor iand 255) + FTHexByte((iColor iand 65280) / 256) + FTHexByte((iColor iand 16711680) / 65536))
End_Function

// The web host backdrop - the twin of --dfr-bg-page.
Function FTWebBg Global Returns Integer
    If (giFTThemeMode = CI_FTThemeLight) ;
        Function_Return clLightWebBg
    Function_Return clDarkWebBg
End_Function

// The ordinary native-view grey - the twin of --dfr-bg-card-hi.
Function FTViewBg Global Returns Integer
    If (giFTThemeMode = CI_FTThemeLight) ;
        Function_Return clLightViewBg
    Function_Return clDarkViewBg
End_Function

// The flat theme ground.
Function FTThemeBg Global Returns Integer
    If (giFTThemeMode = CI_FTThemeLight) ;
        Function_Return clLightTheme
    Function_Return clDarkTheme
End_Function

// Text on any of the above - the twin of --dfr-ink.
Function FTThemeInk Global Returns Integer
    If (giFTThemeMode = CI_FTThemeLight) ;
        Function_Return clLightThemeText
    Function_Return clDarkThemeText
End_Function

/* THE WEBVIEW2 COMPOSITOR BACKGROUND - the layer the colour probe could not reach
   (2026-08-15). Three painters stack under every FT page: the wrapper CONTROL's background
   (piBackColor -> ComBackColor - turned red under the probe, so that knob works), the
   framework page's body (dark via application.css), and the WebView2 compositor's own
   DefaultBackgroundColor - which the DataFlex wrapper does not expose, defaults to WHITE,
   and is what paints the freshly exposed area during a live resize before the page
   relayouts. That is the stripe that survived every dialog-side fix.

   Microsoft's documented escape hatch is the process-wide environment variable
   WEBVIEW2_DEFAULT_BACKGROUND_COLOR, read when a WebView2 ENVIRONMENT is created - so it
   must be set before the first browser control binds. ApplyFTTheme calls this from every
   host's construction, and construction precedes binding; the flag makes it once-only.
   The value is 8-digit AARRGGBB hex: FF (opaque) and FTWebBg's colour, from its Define.

   PROBE 2 VERDICT (2026-08-15): setting this env var to RED changed nothing on Nils's machine
   - the white was the framework PAGE BODY, fixed by the VirtualHtml override in cFTThemeHost_mixin.pkg.
   Kept anyway: it is correct, free, and covers the compositor on machines where it does land. */
Global_Variable Boolean gbFTDefaultBgSet
Move False to gbFTDefaultBgSet

External_Function WV2_SetEnvironmentVariable "SetEnvironmentVariableW" Kernel32.dll ;
    WString sName WString sValue Returns Integer

Procedure ApplyWebView2DefaultBackground Global
    Integer iVoid
    If (gbFTDefaultBgSet) ;
        Procedure_Return
    Move True to gbFTDefaultBgSet
    Move (WV2_SetEnvironmentVariable("WEBVIEW2_DEFAULT_BACKGROUND_COLOR", "FF" + FTColorHex(FTWebBg()))) to iVoid
End_Procedure

// The CodeJock chrome - command bars, dialog status bars, context menus. CodeJock themes itself
// natively rather than through CSS, so it needs its own switch: hardcoding
// xtpThemeVisualStudio2017Dark left every native panel and every themed group dark on a light page
// (Nils 2026-08-13: "the program settings dialog is still dark" - that dialog is all native
// CodeJock controls, so the palette never reached it).
//
// The xtp* constants come from cCJCommandBarSystem.pkg and cCJGridControl.pkg, Used at the top of
// this package. Until 2026-09-23 it relied on every program having Used cRDCCJCommandBarSystem.pkg
// above it, which another workspace would not know to do.
//
// CodeJock reads peVisualTheme when the control REALIZES, so a change needs a program restart -
// the same restart the rest of the theme already asks for.
Function FTCJTheme Global Returns Integer
    If (giFTThemeMode = CI_FTThemeLight) ;
        Function_Return xtpThemeVisualStudio2022Light
    Function_Return xtpThemeVisualStudio2017Dark
End_Function

// The grid chrome, a separate CodeJock enumeration from the command-bar one above.
Function FTCJGridTheme Global Returns Integer
    If (giFTThemeMode = CI_FTThemeLight) ;
        Function_Return xtpGridThemeVisualStudio2012Light
    Function_Return xtpGridThemeVisualStudio2012Dark
End_Function
